Description
MBIS Ibadan is seeking experienced and capable Associate Teachers to join our primary teaching team. We are looking for teachers who already possess sound classroom teaching skills, secure subject knowledge and experience working with primary-aged pupils.
At MBIS, Associate Teachers are expected tobring existing teaching competence to the roleand will be mentored and supported to adapt to our British curriculum, teaching resources, assessment systems, classroom routines and professional expectations.
Essential Experience and Qualifications
Applicants should have:
Bachelor’s Degree or PGDE as a minimum qualification with a minimum of three (3) years’ relevant primary classroom teaching experience;
Experience teaching primary-aged pupils;
Secure knowledge of the primary curriculum, particularly English, Mathematics and Science;
Strong spoken and written English;
Good classroom organisation and behaviour-management skills;
Good computer literacy; and
Clear and legible handwriting
Applicants must be Ibadan-based or able to commute reliably to our school off Jericho, Ibadan. MBIS does not provide staff accommodation or relocation expenses.
Qualifications alone will not be sufficient.
Who We Are Looking For
We are looking for teachers who can demonstrate that they can:
Plan and prepare purposeful lessons;
Teach rather than simply present information;
Explain concepts clearly and accurately;
Use effective questioning;
Model work clearly using the board and appropriate resources;
Maintain appropriate classroom routines and pupil engagement;
Mark and provide appropriate feedback;
Follow curriculum sequences and agreed lesson plans;
Manage time effectively;
Prepare independently and arrive ready to teach;
Receive professional feedback positively and implement it; and
Work reliably without constant supervision.
We are particularly interested in teachers who are competent, teachable and professionally reliable.
What MBIS will Provide
Successful Associate Teachers will receive structured support to adapt to the MBIS environment, including orientation to our curriculum, resources and assessment systems, mentoring, classroom observation, professional feedback and opportunities for professional development.
Mentoring is intended to support adaptation and professional development, not to provide basic training in classroom teaching.

Requirements
A Ph.D. in the relevant discipline, or a Master's degree with at least two (2) years of cognate experience;
Emerging evidence of scholarship through publications.

As an AI Enablement Engineer at FairMoney, you will help drive the adoption of AI-assisted engineering practices across our technology teams. You will work closely with engineering squads to identify opportunities where AI can improve development workflows, developer productivity, automation, and the overall software delivery process.
This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys building, experimenting, automating, and working directly with engineers to turn new AI capabilities into practical engineering solutions.
If you are passionate about AI, developer tooling, automation, and improving the way software teams build and deliver products, we want you to join our team!
We are looking forward to having you work on:
Supporting the adoption of AI-assisted engineering practices across engineering squads;
Building scripts, automations, and developer tools that improve engineering productivity;
Working directly with engineers to identify and implement practical AI use cases across development workflows;
Experimenting with AI coding tools and agents and developing reusable workflows and best practices;
Providing hands-on support to squads and continuously improving AI adoption across the engineering organisation.
Our technical Stack
Our customer-facing product is an Android application;
It communicates with Ruby on Rails or Go-lang backends (Sidekiq, RSpec);
Our ML pipeline is API-Flask (Python);
We are hosted on AWS: Kubernetes, SNS, SQS, Lambdas, RDS Aurora MySQL and PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, S3, and Kinesis;
Prototype of a data warehouse on GCP (GCS, BigQuery, Cloud Composer);
We run our CI/CD pipeline with GitHub Actions;
AI-assisted development and developer productivity tooling.
Basic Qualifications
3+ years of experience in software engineering, developer tooling, automation, or a related technical role;
Hands-on experience with AI-assisted software development and modern AI coding tools;
Strong scripting and automation skills, with proficiency in at least one programming language such as Python, Go, JavaScript, or Ruby;
Experience building internal tools, automation, or developer workflows;
Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to translate engineering challenges into practical technical solutions;
Willingness to work directly with engineering squads and support them hands-on.
Preferred Qualifications
Experience working with AI coding assistants, AI agents, LLM-based developer tools, or similar technologies;
Experience building developer tooling or platforms that improve engineering productivity;
Experience integrating APIs and third-party tools into engineering workflows;
Knowledge of software engineering practices across the full development lifecycle, including coding standards, code reviews, source control, testing, CI/CD, and operations;
Experience working with cloud providers, preferably AWS, alternatively GCP/Azure;
Familiarity with microservices and modern software development architectures;
