Building and supporting reliable distributed systems and backend services;
Working closely with Product, Risk, Compliance, and other engineering teams to deliver effective identity and KYC solutions;
Participating in code reviews and contributing to engineering standards and best practices;
Identifying and resolving performance, scalability, reliability, and security issues;
Using AI-assisted development tools and modern engineering practices to improve productivity and delivery.
Our Technical Stack
Our customer-facing product is an Android application;
It communicates with Ruby on Rails or Go-lang backends (Sidekiq, RSpec);
Our ML pipeline is API-Flask (Python);
We are hosted on AWS: Kubernetes, SNS, SQS, Lambdas, RDS Aurora MySQL and PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, S3, and Kinesis;
Prototype of a data warehouse on GCP (GCS, BigQuery, Cloud Composer);
We run our CI/CD pipeline with GitHub Actions.
Basic Qualifications
4+ years of professional experience in backend software development;
Experience building backend services and working with distributed systems;
Experience working with Go, or strong experience in another backend language with a willingness to transition to Go;
Good understanding of software engineering principles, system design, testing, CI/CD, and production operations;
Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail;
Good verbal and written communication skills;
Experience working effectively within cross-functional engineering teams.
Preferred Qualifications
Experience working in Identity, KYC, authentication, fraud prevention, onboarding, or related domains;
Experience in fintech, banking, payments, or other financial services environments;
Experience with Go and Go-based backend systems;
Familiarity with microservices, event-driven architectures, and distributed systems;
Experience working with AWS or other major cloud platforms;
Experience using AI coding assistants, LLM-based developer tools, or AI-assisted development workflows.
