Ref Code: PMDT/INNO/SEPT/2026
Role Summary:
AB Microfinance Bank Nigeria is seeking a Product Manager, Digital Transformation to own the end-to-end management of approved digital products within the Innovation Department. The role ensures products solve genuine customer and business problems, are delivered effectively and achieve measurable adoption and business outcomes.
Key Responsibilities:
Own the product vision, objectives and roadmap for assigned digital products;
Convert approved opportunities into product concepts, roadmaps and prioritized backlogs;
Manage product backlog, priorities, user stories and release plans;
Work with the Business Analyst, Business, IT and vendors to translate requirements into deliverable product increments.
Coordinate delivery across discovery, design, development, testing, launch and continuous improvement;
Define product KPIs, adoption targets and customer/business outcomes;
Monitor customer feedback, product performance and market developments.
Requirements:
3-5+ years relevant experience with proven digital product management and delivery.
Banking, Fintech, Microfinance, Payments or digital financial services experience is strongly preferred.
Bachelor’s degree in Business, Economics, Technology, Engineering or related discipline.
Product discovery, roadmap and backlog management; Agile/scrum experience.
Customer journey and product experience understanding, business and financial acumen.
Working knowledge of APIs, digital channels and system integration.
Ability to use data and customer feedback to make product decisions; Product management or Agile/scrum certification an advantage.
Performance Measures:
Products/features delivered against roadmap; time to market;
Digital product adoption and usage;
Customer satisfaction and journey completion;
Product revenue, savings or other approved business benefits.
Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.

Description
We’re looking for a Portfolio Analyst to help us scale and optimize our credit portfolio.
You’ll work hands-on with portfolio metrics, risk strategies, and pricing, collaborating closely with Product and Data Science to turn data into clear, impactful decisions. The scope of responsibilities will include:
Responsibilities
Credit Portfolio Management:
Analysis and monitoring of key portfolio metrics: FPD, PD, LGD, NPL, Surplus;
LTV assessment and active participation in product pricing;
Development of customer segmentation strategies (e.g., by risk levels, products, acquisition channels);
Assessment of the impact of internal initiatives on financial results;
Optimization of the portfolio structure (balancing high-yield and low-risk loans).
Risk Management:
Monitoring of risk concentration (e.g., by regions, products, borrower segments);
Adjustment of credit policy based on default and early repayment data;
Development and improvement of processes related to loan origination.
Collaboration with the Data Science Team:
Formulation of requirements for scoring models (e.g., calibration of PD models);
Analysis of scoring card performance and proposals for their improvement;
Work with cash flow forecasting models.
Requirements
3+ years of experience in analytics or portfolio analytics;
Higher education, preferably in a technical or economics-related field;
Strong understanding of credit risks and metrics: PD, NPL, FPD, SPD, Roll Rate, CoR;
Knowledge and practical application of probability theory and mathematical statistics;
Proficiency with analytical tools:
Excel (advanced formulas, pivot tables);
SQL (window functions, subqueries);
Experience working with Python (basic level: NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn);
Knowledge of regulatory requirements applicable to MFIs/Banks.
Nice to Have:
Experience with Big Data and BI systems;
Basic understanding of ML models (interpretation of scoring results);
Knowledge of financial models and statements (NPV, DCF, P&L);
Experience with A/B testing;
Knowledge of MFI/Banking products: microloans, credit cards, credit lines.
Benefits
Remote work from anywhere in the world
Performance bonus, paid vacations and day-offs, personal development plan
Purpose: shape the future of fintech in Nigeria with products that reach millions, backed by a competitive salary
Growth: thrive in a fast paced work environment with flexibility, collaboration, and access to cutting-edge tools
Join a diverse, inclusive team where all voices are valued, and professional growth is a priority.
